  "dct_description_sm": [
    "We evaluated the presence and concentration of 4 types of UV-protectants (carotenoids, scytonemin, mycosporine-like amino acids (MAAs) and melanins) in 12 commonly occurring crustacean species from 27 freshwater bodies in northern Canada and Alaska. In addition to providing a measure of UV protection, the pigments also indicate zooplankton food sources and potential benthicpelagic coupling."
